@@@ note
A literal U+0001 in the source must not be read as the in-band hard-break marker and turned
into a real hard break. The byte below is a real U+0001 — it will look like nothing, or like
a control picture, depending on your editor. See #9.

@@@ input
before  after

@@@ wrap 80
before after

@@@ unwrap
before after

@@@ html-drift
The sentinel byte is dropped rather than preserved, so the rendered output loses it. That is
the intended trade: U+0001 carries no meaning in CommonMark, and keeping it would leave the
in-band hard-break marker ambiguous.
